{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"The first tree differential found a test-oracle issue, not a translation divergence: when `data == NULL`, C initializes only `data[0]` and leaves the remaining 255 malloc bytes indeterminate, so raw comparison beyond the terminating NUL is invalid and differs even across two C allocations. I’m narrowing node-data comparison to the C string’s observable bytes through its first NUL; non-null strings of length 255 or more still compare the full 256-byte field."}}
